      "tokens": 9536,
      "seconds": 13.08,
      "answer": "When CBACT04C applies interest, the cycle credit (WS-MONTHLY-INT) is computed as the product of the transaction category balance (TRAN-CAT-BAL) and the discount interest rate (DIS-INT-RATE), divided by 1200. This amount is then added to the total interest (WS-TOTAL-INT). A transaction record is written to the transaction file (TRANACT-FILE) with the transaction type set to '01' (indicating an interest transaction), the account ID, the transaction amount (WS-MONTHLY-INT), and other transaction details. If the write operation is successful, the transaction record is updated in the account file (ACCOUNT-FILE) to reflect the cycle credit.",
